# The Jolly Balloon Man copying a Sacred Cat token made by embalm (CR 707.9b, 702.128a): embalm's exception already states the
# token's color, white (and that it has no mana cost), and that stated value is part of its copiable values, so "red in
# addition to its other colors" makes the copy white and red, not red alone (`Copiable::with_color` over colors an earlier
# exception states). Turn 1: Sacred Cat and Jolly off Black Lotus and the Moxen; Bot1's own Lightning Bolt kills the Cat,
# which is embalmed with the Lotus's last white. Turn 3: Jolly copies the token.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Ruby
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Sacred Cat
The Jolly Balloon Man
Lightning Bolt
Plains x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Hand.Sacred Cat.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.The Jolly Balloon Man.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Sacred Cat)
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Graveyard.Sacred Cat.Activate(Ability: Embalm)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Sacred Cat.Colors = White
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.The Jolly Balloon Man.Activate(Sacred Cat)
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Sacred Cat#1.Colors = White
Bot1.Battlefield.Sacred Cat#2.Colors = Red; White
Bot1.Battlefield.Sacred Cat#2.Subtypes = Balloon; Cat; Zombie
Bot1.Battlefield.Sacred Cat#2.ManaValue = 0
